hadiths[50]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1459","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The sun and moon are two signs of Allah (SWT)"
"1460","Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah said:""While I was (practicing) shooting some arrows in Al-Madinah"
"1461","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The sun and moon do not become eclipsed for death or birth of anyone"
"1462","It was narrated that Abu Mas'ud said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The sun and the moon do not become eclipsed for the death or birth of anyone"
"1463","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The sun and moon are two signs of Allah(ﷺ)"
"1464","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""We were sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) when the sun became eclipsed. He leapt up"
"1465","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:""The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"1466","Urwah bin Az-Zubair narrated that 'Aishah"
"1467","It was narrated from Tawus from Ibn Abbas"
"1468","It was narrated from Tawus from Ibn Abbas that:The Prophet (ﷺ) prayed when there was an eclipse. He recited then he bowed"
"1469","It was narrated from Kathir bin Abbas"
"1470","Ata said:""I heard Ubaid bin Umair say: 'Someone whom I trust'- and I think he meant Aishah- told me: There was an eclipse of the sun during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He led the people in prayer and stood for a very long time"
"1471","It was narrated fom 'Ata from Ibn 'Umair"
"1472","It was narrated from Ibn Shihab rom 'Urwah bin Az-Zubair"
"1473","It was narrated from Az-Zuhri"
"1474","It was narrated from Hisham bin 'Urwah"
"1475","It was narrated from Yahya bin Sa'eed that :'Amrah told him that Aishah told her that a Jewish woman came to her and said: ""May Allah protect you from the torment of the grave."" Aishah said: ""O Messenger of Allah"
"1476","Amrah said:""I heard Aishah say: 'A Jewish woman came to me begging"
"1477","It was narrated from Aishah that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed during an eclipse in a shaded area near Zamzam"
"1478","It was narrated that Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:""The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a very hot day. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led his companions in prayer"
"1479","It was narrated that Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"1480","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""The sun was eclipsed and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) bowed twice and prostrated twice"
"1481","Abu Hafs"
"1482","Abdullah bin 'Amr said:""The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) got up to pray"
"1483","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He stood and led the people in prayer. He stood for a long time"
"1484","Tha'labah bin 'Abbad Al-'Abdi from the people of Al-Basrah narrated that:He attended a Khutbah one day that was delivered by Samurah bin Jundub. In his Khutbah he mentioned a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Samurah bin Jundub said: ""One day a boy from among the Ansar and I were shooting at two targets of ours"
"1485","It was narrated that An-Nu'man bin Bashir said:""The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he rushed out"
"1486","It was narrated that Qabisah bin Mukhariq Al-Hilali said:""There was an eclipse of the sun and at the time we were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in Al-Madinah. He rushed out dragging his garment and prayed two rak'ahs"
"1487","It was narrated from Qabisah Al-Hilali:That there was an eclipse of the sun and the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) prayed two rak'ahs until it ended. Then he said: ""The sun and the moon do not become eclipsed for the death of anyone"
"1488","It was narrated from An-Nu'man bin Bashir that :The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""If there is an eclipse of the sun or the moon"
"1489","It was narrated from An-Nu'man bin Bashir that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed when there was an eclipse of the sun like our prayer"
"1490","It was narrated from An-Nu'man bin Bashir that :The Prophet (ﷺ) came rushing out to the masjid one day when the sun eclipsed"
"1491","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when the sun became eclipsed. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out dragging his garment"
"1492","It was narrated from Abu Bakrah that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed two rak'ahs like this prayer of yours"
"1493","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin Abbas said:""There was an eclipse of the sun and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed and the people with him. He stood for long time reciting something like Surah Al-Baqarah"
"1494","It was narrated from Aishah that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed"
"1495","It was narrated from Samurah that:The Prophet (ﷺ) led them in prayer during an eclipse of the sun"
"1496","It was narrated that Abdullah bin Amr said:""The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed and stood for a long time"
"1497","It was narrated that Aishah said:""There was an eclipse of the sun and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered a man to call out: As-salatu jami'ah (prayer is about to begin in congregation). The people gathered and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led them in prayer. He said the takbir"
"1498","It was narrated that Asma' bint Abi Bakr said:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed during an eclipse. He stood for a long time"
"1499","Aishah said:""The Prophet (ﷺ) went out and the sun became eclipsed. We went out to the apartment and some women gathered around us. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turned to us"
"1500","It was narrated that Aishah said:""There was an eclipse of the sun during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He stood and prayed"
"1501","It was narrated from Samurah that:The Prophet (ﷺ) delivered a Khutbah when the sun eclipsed and he said: 'Amma ba'd (to proceed)"
"1502","It was narrated that Abu Bakrah said:""We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) and the sun became eclipsed. He got up and went to the masjid"
"1503","It was narrated that Abu Musa said:""There was an eclipse of the sun"
"1504","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:""A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"1505","It was narrated from 'Abbad bin Tamim:""Sufyan said: 'I asked 'Abdullah bin Abi Bakr who said: I heard it from Abbad bin Tamim who narrated it from his father"
"1506","It was narrated from Hisham bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah that :His father said: ""So and so sent me to ask him how the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed for rain (Istisqa')."" He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out beseeching and humble"
"1507","It was narrated from Abdullah bin Zaid that:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed for rain wearing a black khamisah"
"1508","It was narrated from Hisham binIshaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah that:His father said: ""I asked Ibn 'Abbas how the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed for rain. He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out (dressed) in a state of humility"